## 9. Minimum decisions
**Before the pilot (before the first pilot call):** SF counting convention and the `f_S` unit (C-04/05); OD-10 basis for the paid pilot calls (C-01); D1 (C-06); D7 (C-11) before the blind check is evaluated; Q-P1 to Q-P4 as a safe-stop policy (C-12..C-15); owner authorization and Step 9 evidence (human). **Before the FZ hash (which precedes the first pilot call):** the FZ hash contract (C-03); kappa and the re-code values (C-02/C-09); D2 (C-07); D3 (C-08); timeout meaning (C-16); confirmation of the Step 8 choices (C-28). **Later:** resume (C-17), PRD-6 before the record is written (C-18), token measurement before the main run, coding eligibility before coding, P-3 item 1.

## 10. Final readiness criteria
All items of `MASTER_PILOT_READINESS_CHECKLIST.md` sections 1-3 marked done with the evidence named there; every PENDING decision in section 9 "before the pilot" adopted by a record entry with a name and a date; code patches for adopted rules merged with their regression tests passing; the gate check without `--live` printing "gates open" for the right reasons; no gate opened by assumption. This document does not claim readiness.
